From 81083da344d5d4cd24abde97ccfa3e7e467dde6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:51:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(gpui): tell an editable leaf when the platform
 realizes it

An editable leaf that paints its own caret over a caret the platform is
already drawing shows two. It cannot work out which case it is in, because
nothing else about the leaf differs: identity, layout, focus, state and
lifetime stay GPUI's on either path, which is the property that lets one
element implementation serve both.

`PlatformNativeElement` is that one question and nothing more. Placement
already flows through the platform's existing caret bounds, so a
create/place/destroy protocol would add a second authority for one
rectangle without answering anything the leaf cannot already see.

Every platform answers `None` by default, so this compiles everywhere and
changes nothing until a platform overrides it.
---
 crates/gpui/src/platform.rs | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 crates/gpui/src/window.rs   | 14 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs b/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs
